<Vertical id="uk_12_s6" title="A second journey">
<Markdown id="uk_12_s6_text">
On another day, Morwenna meets Zofia outside the station with a folder pressed flat against her coat. She has put it inside a plastic bag. The bag advertises oranges.

They walk to the scaffold-site memorial on Tower Hill. Traffic moves beyond the gardens; a delivery rider stops to adjust something at his ankle. Zofia remembers arriving here with a demand that seemed impossible to misunderstand. Record why he refused. She hadn't known how many different ways a person could avoid answering that.

Morwenna takes the folder out of the bag. There is a separate sheet for the annotation and another for the refusal of reversal. The original case summary is reproduced with both.

Zofia looks at the place where Hale used to stand. She can remember the angle of his head when he thought her question had omitted the important part. Remembering it does not put him there.

A gust lifts the top sheet. Morwenna holds its edge, then passes the whole folder over.

Zofia had asked her to come because she did not want to do this alone. Now Morwenna is here, and Zofia wishes she could tell her to go and buy oranges and leave the answer unread for another hour.
</Markdown>
</Vertical>

<Vertical id="uk_12_s7" title="His stated reason">
<Markdown id="uk_12_hale_answer_scene">
