<Vertical id="uk_12_s8" title="The day of the slam">
<Markdown id="uk_12_s8_text">
The day of the slam.

Grace had kept her hand round Zofia's sleeve. Zofia could feel the seam pressing against her wrist. Kit was on her other side. Their mouths moved. She could see when they asked a question because they waited afterwards.

She kept looking back.

They brought her to the Serpentine bank that same day. Ewa was there when they arrived. Grace showed her the messages on her phone, then stepped aside without letting go until Ewa had taken Zofia's hand.

The water was below the bank. Zofia's shoes stayed on the path.

Ewa spread a coat on a bench and sat beside her. There was mud on Kit's trouser leg. Ollie had brought a bag with a split handle, which he held underneath with both hands. Nobody put anything in the water. Nobody tried to take Zofia into it.

Ewa turned so that Zofia could see her face. She pointed to herself, then to the space beside Zofia on the bench. She spoke slowly. Zofia could not hear a word.

She looked over Ewa's shoulder. Grace was standing there with Zofia's bag. The strap had left a red line across her hand.

Ewa waited. Zofia could still feel her fingers.
</Markdown>
</Vertical>

<Vertical id="uk_12_s9" title="The first living answer">
<Markdown id="uk_12_bank_then_scene">
*On the Serpentine bench that day, Ewa keeps her hand round Zofia's cold fingers.*
</Markdown>
<Chat id="uk_12_bank_then" src="silence.chatpeg" clip="bank_then"/>
</Vertical>

<Vertical id="uk_12_s10" title="The bag on the bench">
<Markdown id="uk_12_s10_text">
Now, months later, the bag on the bench belongs to Ewa. It contains bread, a leaking pen in a separate pocket and the printed correction folded inside a clear sleeve. Zofia puts her own papers beside it. Ewa moves them away from the damp patch on the wood.

The Serpentine has little broken ridges across it. Each one catches light, then loses it. A runner comes past breathing hard enough that Zofia hears him before his shoes. Somewhere behind the bench a bicycle bell rings twice.

She has come here with Ewa. There was no search to arrange first, no one to collect on the way.

For a while they watch a crisp packet snag against a twig near the edge. Zofia starts to stand. Ewa catches the back of her coat.

“Leave it. We can tell someone with a grabber.”

Zofia sits down again. The packet keeps tugging at the twig.

She has told her mother about the late answers. She has not told her what she did after reading Hale's, how long she stood there, or what Morwenna asked. Ewa has not filled the gap for her. She unfastens the bag, checks the lid of her water bottle and fastens it again.
</Markdown>
</Vertical>

<Vertical id="uk_12_s11" title="Which part">
<Markdown id="uk_12_bank_now_scene">
*Months later, on the same bank, Ewa closes the shopping bag between them.*
</Markdown>
